# Delmarva Site Handbook (project source of truth)

## When to read it

Before **substantive** work—features, refactors, Contentful/CMS, patterns touching pages/API/i18n, CI or env, analytics or tags, or anything that changes how the app is built or behaves:

1. Skim **`docs/handbook/README.md`** (index and onboarding order).
2. Use **`docs/handbook/llms.md`** to pick the right chapter for the task (task → file map).

Read that chapter and follow its patterns. Repo root **`CLAUDE.md`** aligns with this; do not treat one-off chat context as a substitute for the handbook when the handbook applies.

## Keep docs in sync

If the change would make **`docs/handbook/*.md`** wrong or incomplete (new flows, moved files, component/CMS/parser conventions, env/CI/tags expectations), **update the matching handbook chapter** in the same PR when practical, or in a small follow-up immediately after. Do not leave the handbook stale on purpose.

## When you can skip a full pass

Narrow edits where behavior and documented expectations stay the same—e.g. obvious typos, single-line mechanical fixes—do not require re-reading every chapter.
